# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# The old 2019 URLs 301 to their new homes. These pages have been indexed for
# years; every one of them is a route someone may still arrive on. Do not remove
# them, and do not downgrade any of them to a 302.
#
# Rules are matched top to bottom. Cloudflare Pages allows 2100 static rules; we
# are using a handful. Splats (:splat) are supported.

# --- old page structure --------------------------------------------------
#
# ⚠ /ubytovani IS A REAL PAGE AGAIN AND MUST NOT APPEAR ON THE LEFT HERE.
#
# It briefly redirected to an invented /chalupa. The rename was reverted — the
# path has been indexed since 2019 and the client calls the page `Ubytování` —
# so the rule is gone. If you ever put `/ubytovani` back in the left column
# pointing at a page that then points back, you have built a redirect loop and
# the page will be unreachable rather than merely wrong. Rules match top to
# bottom, so a stale rule here would shadow the real route.
#
# /o-nas goes to the HOMEPAGE, not to /ubytovani, and that is deliberate: the
# old About page held the intro paragraph and the `V okolí naleznete` distance
# list, and both of those are now homepage sections. A redirect should land on
# the content, not on the page with the most similar name.
/o-nas                  /                   301
/o-nas/                 /                   301
/video                  /ubytovani#video    301
/video/                 /ubytovani#video    301
/volne-terminy-a-ceny   /terminy-a-ceny     301
/volne-terminy-a-ceny/  /terminy-a-ceny     301
/tipy-na-vylety         /okoli              301
/tipy-na-vylety/        /okoli              301

# The short-lived /chalupa URL. It existed only between two builds of this
# rebuild and was never linked from anywhere public, but it may sit in a
# bookmark or a crawl queue, so it is retired properly rather than 404ed.
/chalupa                /ubytovani          301
/chalupa/               /ubytovani          301

# --- trailing slashes on surviving routes --------------------------------
# astro.config.mjs sets trailingSlash: 'never'; keep one canonical URL per page.
/kontakt/               /kontakt            301
/galerie/               /galerie            301
/ubytovani/             /ubytovani          301
/terminy-a-ceny/        /terminy-a-ceny     301
/okoli/                 /okoli              301

# --- WordPress leftovers -------------------------------------------------
# The old site was WordPress. These paths are probed constantly by bots and are
# also occasionally still linked; send them home rather than serving a 404 page
# to a crawler.
/wp-content/*           /                301
/wp-includes/*          /                301
/feed                   /                301
/feed/                  /                301

# Note: Pages `_redirects` matches paths, not query strings, so the old
# WordPress search URLs (/?s=…) cannot be caught here. They resolve to `/`
# anyway, which is the right destination.
